   $q$In paragraph 4, Dr. Lindqvist describes a "pristine" map. What does "pristine" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"marked by years of use","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"in perfect, untouched condition","is_correct":true},{"text":"carefully repaired by experts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"very old and valuable","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$in perfect, untouched condition$q$, $q$She restates the word as "perfectly clean and unmarked," so pristine means in perfect, untouched condition. A map with a cup ring is marked by use, which is the opposite of what she describes.$q$, 'draft', '20b7ea01-ca15-5251-9b32-403268cf47d7')
