  ('ea3b173f-6f20-5acf-8ef8-7719ebd74e90', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-context-clues'), null, 'medium',
   $q$In paragraph 3, lichens are "highly susceptible to pollution." Which meaning of "susceptible" does the cause and effect in this paragraph support?$q$, $q$[{"text":"easily affected or harmed by something","is_correct":true},{"text":"protected from something by tree bark","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"likely to spread something to others","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"able to clean something out of the air","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$easily affected or harmed by something$q$, $q$Because lichens absorb what is in the air "straight into their tissues," pollution that a tree can tolerate "may kill" them, so susceptible means easily harmed. Nothing in the paragraph says lichens remove pollution from the air.$q$, 'draft', '731f37bb-eb89-5cb4-98c8-2dc7b0f84d38')
