  ('36348e70-c591-5d19-bf3c-1219105a872f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-context-clues'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 4, the author begins a sentence with "Conversely." What does this word signal about the two parks being described?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The second park shows the opposite situation from the first.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The second park has more lichens than the first one does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The second park is an example that proves the first point.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-contrast"},{"text":"The second park is the cause of the first park's problem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The second park shows the opposite situation from the first.$q$, $q$"Conversely" means in the opposite way, and the sentence it starts describes a park with few lichens and likely pollution, the reverse of the clean park with leafy lichens. It does not add a supporting example, because the second park shows the opposite result.$q$, 'draft', '731f37bb-eb89-5cb4-98c8-2dc7b0f84d38')
