  ('abe167c2-9f59-5842-89ec-d978c755bb18', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-context-clues'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The word "resolve" appears in paragraph 1 and in paragraph 6. How do its meanings differ?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In paragraph 1 it is a verb meaning to show as separate; in paragraph 6 it is a noun meaning determination.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In paragraph 1 it is a noun meaning a clear image; in paragraph 6 it is a verb meaning to stay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-part-of-speech"},{"text":"In paragraph 1 it is a verb meaning to settle an argument; in paragraph 6 it is a noun meaning a solution.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"In both paragraphs it is a verb meaning to make a firm decision about what to do next.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-part-of-speech-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In paragraph 1 it is a verb meaning to show as separate; in paragraph 6 it is a noun meaning determination.$q$, $q$In paragraph 1 the telescope can "resolve" the stars by "separating what looked like a single point of light into two distinct stars," while in paragraph 6 Ines's "stubborn resolve to stay" is her determination. Treating both uses as the same verb misses that the use in paragraph 6 names a quality Ines has.$q$, 'draft', 'a393645a-b240-5a10-8a03-34fcbda295db')
